{
  "fromId": "x",
  "toId": "k_aspirated",
  "preamble": "The voiceless velar fricative [x] is replaced by the aspirated velar stop [kʰ], a fortition that keeps the voiceless velar place and turns continuous friction into a stop with an aspirated release. It arises where /x/ merges with an existing /kʰ/: in Thai the Sukhothai-era letter ฃ, which spelled a distinct velar fricative, fell together with ข [kʰ]; and across Indo-Aryan, Persian and Arabic loans with /x/ are nativized with /kʰ/, regularly in Bengali and outside careful speech in Hindi.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Fortition, Stopping, Aspiration, Merger",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Thai",
      "languageFamily": "Southwestern Tai",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Sukhothai ฃาย (ฃ = velar fricative) 'to sell'",
          "to": "ขาย /kʰaːj˩˩˦/",
          "note": "The Ram Khamhaeng inscription writes eleven words with ฃ; later inscriptions confuse ฃ and ข, and all such words are now spelled with ข [kʰ]. Li (1977) reconstructs the series as Proto-Tai *x; Pittayaporn (2009) reconstructs uvular *q, so the value of ฃ before the merger is debated."
        },
        {
          "from": "Sukhothai ฃวา 'right (side)'",
          "to": "ขวา /kʰwaː˩˩˦/",
          "note": "Obsolete spelling with ฃ replaced by ข."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Hindi",
      "languageFamily": "Indo-Aryan",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "ख़बर /xə.bəɾ/ 'news' (< Persian xabar < Arabic ḵabar)",
          "to": "खबर /kʰə.bəɾ/",
          "note": "Outside careful educated speech the borrowed fricative is replaced by native /kʰ/; the nuqta-less spelling reflects this."
        },
        {
          "from": "ख़राब /xə.ɾɑːb/ 'bad' (< Persian xarāb)",
          "to": "खराब /kʰə.ɾɑːb/",
          "note": "Same substitution; Wiktionary lists both pronunciations."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Bengali",
      "languageFamily": "Indo-Aryan",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Persian xabar 'news'",
          "to": "খবর [ˈkʰɔboɾ]",
